{"term":"thaw","senses":[{"id":"kaikki:bb44517a85c1200d95","definition":"To gradually cause (something frozen, such as earth, ice, or snow) to melt or soften by raising the temperature.","example":"Sette the potte to the fyre to thawe the water: […]","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"transitive","wordFamily":["dethaw","freeze-thaw","postthaw","rethaw","thawable","thawed","thawer","thawing","thawingly","thawless","thaw out","unthaw","unthawed","thawy"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/thaw#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:9d55075510306466d6","definition":"To gradually cause (someone or something that is very cold) to warm up.","example":"[M]y very lippes might freeze to my teeth, my tongue to the roofe of my mouth, my heart in my belly, ere I ſhould come by a fire to thavv me, […]","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"transitive","wordFamily":["dethaw","freeze-thaw","postthaw","rethaw","thawable","thawed","thawer","thawing","thawingly","thawless","thaw out","unthaw","unthawed","thawy"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/thaw#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:480c501026330dc967","definition":"To cause (something inactive) to become active; also, to cause (something unfeeling) to have feelings.","example":"[N]ovv my loue is thavv'd, / VVhich like a vvaxen Image 'gainſt a fire / Beares no impreſſion of the thing it vvas.","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"figuratively","register":"figuratively, transitive","wordFamily":["dethaw","freeze-thaw","postthaw","rethaw","thawable","thawed","thawer","thawing","thawingly","thawless","thaw out","unthaw","unthawed","thawy"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/thaw#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:570ae0ad90e6ca4687","definition":"To cause (someone or their feelings that are reserved or unfriendly) to become friendly or gentle.","example":"","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"figuratively","register":"figuratively, transitive","wordFamily":["dethaw","freeze-thaw","postthaw","rethaw","thawable","thawed","thawer","thawing","thawingly","thawless","thaw out","unthaw","unthawed","thawy"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/thaw#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:bf5db1dba5ee2e8011","definition":"To cause (something rigid) to become limp.","example":"\"Speak aloud, my lord,\" said Elizabeth, \"and at farther distance, so please you—your breath thaws our ruff. What have you to ask of us?\"","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"archaic, figuratively, rare","register":"archaic, figuratively, rare, transitive","wordFamily":["dethaw","freeze-thaw","postthaw","rethaw","thawable","thawed","thawer","thawing","thawingly","thawless","thaw out","unthaw","unthawed","thawy"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/thaw#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:63005fb33ab438b749","definition":"Of something frozen, such as earth, ice, or snow: to gradually melt or soften as a result of the temperature being raised.","example":"the ice thaws","pos":"verb","synonyms":["de-ice"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"intransitive","wordFamily":["dethaw","freeze-thaw","postthaw","rethaw","thawable","thawed","thawer","thawing","thawingly","thawless","thaw out","unthaw","unthawed","thawy"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/thaw#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:cbf2aeb3acfe48889e","definition":"Of someone or something that is very cold: to gradually warm up.","example":"The bog's green harper, thawing from his sleep, / Twangs a hoarse note and tried a shortened leap; […]","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"intransitive","wordFamily":["dethaw","freeze-thaw","postthaw","rethaw","thawable","thawed","thawer","thawing","thawingly","thawless","thaw out","unthaw","unthawed","thawy"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/thaw#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:dcbdf4945369ac9790","definition":"With the dummy pronoun it: of the weather: to become sufficiently warm for ice, snow, etc., to melt.","example":"It’s beginning to thaw.","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"impersonal","register":"impersonal, intransitive","wordFamily":["dethaw","freeze-thaw","postthaw","rethaw","thawable","thawed","thawer","thawing","thawingly","thawless","thaw out","unthaw","unthawed","thawy"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/thaw#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:dba397b00001ddf05a","definition":"Of a person or their feelings that are reserved or unfriendly: to become friendly or gentle.","example":"Her anger has thawed.","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"figuratively","register":"figuratively, intransitive","wordFamily":["dethaw","freeze-thaw","postthaw","rethaw","thawable","thawed","thawer","thawing","thawingly","thawless","thaw out","unthaw","unthawed","thawy"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.or